        "text_eng": "Statistical analysis shows that in the advanced countries the level of financing towards health services is making little impact on the health of their populations. Though some countries spend six times as much per head on the health facilities and countries spending only half as much, life expectancies of their populations are almost same. Thus it is meaningless to say that the health of population depends in the level of finances spent per head.\nSelect the underlying assumption with respect to above argument.",
